  'worldGen.safeToLeaveHold': 'The concrete hold promise paired directly under worldGen.safeToLeave (ux-run3 myth-b965d): permission alone left the loop open — this one short sentence says the world will be held right here for the player\'s return. Same quiet mono register; one terse sentence, no em dashes.',
  'worldGen.stagePosition': 'The stage-scoped line on the world-gen status card: WHICH watched stage is underway, explicitly positioned so stage scope is never conflated with overall time (ux-run2 myth-uz1bn — a bare stage label beside a percent read as overall progress). Interpolates {{current}} + {{total}} (the watched-stage position) and {{stage}} (the friendly stage label from worldGen.stage.*). A label·value row (the middot, not an em dash), e.g. "Stage 2 of 4 · Settling people and places".',
  'worldGen.waitQuietly': 'The quiet return link on the world-gen status card (live graph view) back to the calm loading screen — the calm screen exists precisely for the player who does not want minutes of animation, so watching must not be a one-way door (ux-run2 myth-t11az). Mono text-link register matching the entry CTA\'s quietness; terse, ~2-3 words, e.g. "Wait quietly". NOT "…instead" (ux-run3 myth-fi1v1: the trailing adverb dangles — the link already sits beside the thing it is an alternative to).',
  'worldGen.loadingLabel': 'Screen-reader label on the Spinner of the pre-entity world-gen loading screen (act one of the two-act flow) — the busy announcement AT hears while the prep stages run. Terse, ~2-4 words.',
  'worldGen.watch': 'Label on the watch button that appears on the loading screen once entities start streaming — pressing it swaps to the live graph view (the deliberate beat; generation keeps running regardless; formerly worldGen.reveal — renamed because "reveal" now names the wiki-reveal moment). Brand-voiced, ~4-6 words, e.g. "watch your world be born".',
  'worldGen.a11y.entityList': 'SCREEN-READER-ONLY aria-label (never shown) for the hidden list of entities that have appeared so far during world generation — the generation graph canvas is aria-hidden, so this list is a SR user\'s only way to read what has taken shape. Plain and orienting, ~4-6 words, e.g. "what has taken shape so far".',
  'worldGen.a11y.entities': 'SCREEN-READER-ONLY live-region tally (never shown) announcing how many entities have appeared during world generation; {{count}} is interpolated. Coalesced so a burst announces once. Plain and factual, ~3-5 words, e.g. "{{count}} have taken shape".',
  'worldGen.flavor1': 'Flavor line 1 of 20 on the pre-entity world-gen loading screen. The label cycles through the twenty lines every ~3s in RANDOM order (a shuffled cycle — every line shows once before any repeats; Claude-Code-"thinking" style) while the prep stages run. Short playful loading message, brand-voiced (Ghibli-not-Marvel, no hype), ~3-6 words. Miklos writes the set.',
  'worldGen.flavor2': 'Flavor line 2 of 20 on the pre-entity world-gen loading screen (see worldGen.flavor1). Short playful loading message, ~3-6 words.',
